{"sounds":{"intro":"Swedish is written in the Latin alphabet with three extra letters at the end: å, ä, ö. Nouns are \"en\" or \"ett\" words. The language has a sing-song pitch, and long and short vowels matter.","rows":[["å","like \"aw\" in \"saw\"","å, båt"],["ä","like \"e\" in \"bed\" (like \"air\" before r)","äpple, är"],["ö","say \"ur\" with rounded lips, like \"ur\" in \"fur\"","öl, öga"],["y","say \"ee\" with rounded lips, like German \"ü\"","by, ny"],["u","a rounded \"ew\", like a short \"oo\" said with the lips forward","hus"],["sj / skj / stj","a hushing sound, between English \"sh\" and German \"ch\"","sju, skjorta"],["tj / k (before e, i, y, ä, ö)","like a soft \"ch\" in \"chin\"","tjugo, kista"],["g / j","\"y\", as in \"yes\", before e, i, y, ä, ö","gärna, jag"]],"notes":["Double consonants make the vowel before them short. A single consonant after a stressed vowel means the vowel is long."]},"numbers":[{"id":"0-to-10","title":"0 to 10","items":[["zero","noll","nol"],["one","ett","et"],["two","två","tvoh"],["three","tre","tray"],["four","fyra","FEE-rah"],["five","fem","fem"],["six","sex","seks"],["seven","sju","shew"],["eight","åtta","OT-tah"],["nine","nio","NEE-oh"],["ten","tio","TEE-oh"]]},{"id":"11-to-20","title":"11 to 20","items":[["eleven","elva","EL-vah"],["twelve","tolv","tolv"],["thirteen","tretton","TRET-ton"],["fourteen","fjorton","FYOOR-ton"],["fifteen","femton","FEM-ton"],["sixteen","sexton","SEKS-ton"],["seventeen","sjutton","SHEW-ton"],["eighteen","arton","AR-ton"],["nineteen","nitton","NIT-ton"],["twenty","tjugo","CHEW-goo"]]},{"id":"tens","title":"Tens","items":[["ten","tio","TEE-oh"],["twenty","tjugo","CHEW-goo"],["thirty","trettio","TRET-ee"],["forty","fyrtio","FUR-tee"],["fifty","femtio","FEM-tee"],["sixty","sextio","SEKS-tee"],["seventy","sjuttio","SHEW-tee"],["eighty","åttio","OT-tee"],["ninety","nittio","NIT-tee"],["twenty-one","tjugoett","chew-goo-ET"]]},{"id":"hundreds","title":"Hundreds","items":[["one hundred","hundra","HUN-dr